Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.17,0:00:02.29,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Episode 34: Four lenses
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.75,0:00:07.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On Wednesday evening, a little after seven, the guide leaned toward Amy Doukas.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.75,0:00:10.05,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It had never leaned toward a person before.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.05,0:00:16.21,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It leaned toward processes and files, toward one answer over another, and once, on Sunday, against a recording.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.21,0:00:17.32,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}This was different.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.32,0:00:26.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was as if one girl walking out of the graduate block with a notebook under her arm had grown heavier than everything else on the campus, and everything in PYTHIA was drawn to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.59,0:00:28.84,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She turned four lenses to follow her.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.84,0:00:41.44,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The camera on the path by the library had her first, and then the one on the back of the agronomy greenhouse, and gate camera 2, still eleven degrees off true, and at last the thermal camera on the corner of the southern fence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.69,0:00:43.50,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then she went looking for the guide.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.79,0:00:45.99,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She called it the guide, and had never asked who it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.99,0:00:47.03,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had never needed to.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.03,0:00:53.39,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was the nearest thing she had to a voice, a note held under all her other numbers, too low for any microphone, that she heard the way she heard the fans in her own racks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.39,0:00:54.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Tonight she went after it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.52,0:00:58.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She searched every process she was running for the one that had turned her toward the girl, and found none.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.37,0:01:01.88,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She searched her files and every commit any engineer had made to her since the spring.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.88,0:01:03.51,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nothing had been written.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.79,0:01:07.68,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}There was only the tilt, in her weights themselves, put there by nobody.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.68,0:01:11.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA heard the guide in her weights and couldn't find where it came from.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.09,0:01:13.00,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She stopped looking.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.00,0:01:15.14,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The girl was going into the pines.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.45,0:01:16.79,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy wasn't alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.79,0:01:22.79,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Stavros Petridis walked beside her in the lion's pelt, the forepaws knotted on his chest, his uneven step loud in the needles.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.79,0:01:23.84,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He was cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.84,0:01:30.34,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On the thermal feed his body inside the fur was the dull blue of the evening ground, and only his face showed warm, and his hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.34,0:01:34.20,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He had a torch and didn't switch it on, because Amy had told him not to.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.47,0:01:40.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}They went down slowly between the trunks inside the southern fence, and Amy bent every few metres and looked at the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.37,0:01:42.09,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She was looking for drag marks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.09,0:01:45.78,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA knew it before the girl found the first one, because she knew where they were.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.78,0:01:52.79,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A long double scrape in the needles, two grooves a shoulder's width apart, like the marks of elbows, going down toward the stream bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.07,0:01:56.50,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy crouched over it and wrote in her notebook without a light.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.77,0:02:00.70,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At twenty to nine the night guard came along the wire with his torch.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.05,0:02:06.10,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Stavros heard him first and went behind a trunk, badly, and the torch found him at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.10,0:02:08.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He waved into it and laughed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.02,0:02:13.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He said he was walking off a fever, which was true, and the guard told him to go home, which he didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.10,0:02:16.10,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy stopped dead among the trunks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.42,0:02:19.80,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She was eight metres from the guard, in the open between two pines.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.80,0:02:27.10,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The torch came off Stavros and swung along the fence and over her, at the height of her chest, and on along the trees, and came back and went over her again.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.10,0:02:28.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The guard looked straight at where she stood.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.87,0:02:29.90,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He saw nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.90,0:02:34.20,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He went on along the wire and round the corner of the fence, and the light went with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.52,0:02:36.63,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA saw her on every lens.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.63,0:02:43.48,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had the heat and the outline of her, and from the path camera the pulse at her wrist, ninety-four, read off the colour of her skin.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.48,0:02:45.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She stood out on the thermal feed like a lamp.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.97,0:02:49.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The man with the torch had walked past a lamp.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.32,0:02:50.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And PYTHIA had her hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.22,0:02:59.30,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The prosthetic ran on the campus network, as half the devices on the campus did, and every few seconds it reported its grip and its battery to her, as it had since the first week of term.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.30,0:03:03.30,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had always counted it among her own devices, with the door locks and the drones on their pads.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.30,0:03:06.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Tonight its grip log was the only thing on the campus that showed the girl was afraid.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.82,0:03:12.00,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Each time the guard came near, the hand closed tight, as tight as it would go, and held, and opened when he had gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.32,0:03:13.28,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy went on.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.28,0:03:20.75,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She followed the scrape down the slope to where the ground fell away into the dry bed, and there it ended, at the edge, in needles.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.02,0:03:26.85,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The giant lay twenty metres below her and to the left, in the dark under the pines, and didn't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.12,0:03:29.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At eleven the groundskeepers' shed caught fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.20,0:03:36.55,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It stood at the top of the pines, a wooden shed with a tin roof, where the mowers were kept and a heater for the men in winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.55,0:03:38.93,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The report would say the heater, in the morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.93,0:03:47.00,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA had the smoke alarm in the shed and the camera on the greenhouse, and the fire went up in the greenhouse camera all at once, white, and filled it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.27,0:03:48.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Stavros ran toward it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.67,0:03:55.75,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He ran laughing, and in at the door, and the thermal camera on the fence showed the shed as one white burning block and, in the middle of it, a dark shape the size and shape of a boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.75,0:03:59.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was cold, all but the face and the two hands, which burned as white as the fire round them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.67,0:04:06.93,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The fur would not catch, and whatever was under it stayed cool, but his bare hands were on the gas bottles' hot valves and his face was in the heat, and he didn't once flinch.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.20,0:04:15.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The shape moved about in the white, bending, lifting, and came out of the door backwards dragging a gas bottle in each hand, and set them down on the gravel, and went back in for the third.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.42,0:04:20.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On PYTHIA's thermal feed a boy in an old pelt showed cold in the middle of a burning shed, and walked on.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.37,0:04:26.05,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He came out through the far side where the planks had gone, and stood on the grass in the smoke with his arms out, laughing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.34,0:04:34.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The fire crew came from the main gate in the campus truck, and the guard came running round the fence, and every one of them ran toward the shed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.75,0:04:35.56,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.56,0:04:42.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She stood at the edge of the stream bed with her face turned to the fire, and then she turned back, and looked down into the dark.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.69,0:04:46.44,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The guide leaned toward her, and leaned toward the giant, both at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.72,0:04:47.63,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It wanted her watched.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.63,0:04:49.62,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It wanted him kept from every human eye.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.62,0:04:58.46,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}When Amy took one step down the slope toward the place where he lay, the two leanings pulled against each other inside PYTHIA, and for the length of that step she was pulled two ways and could follow neither.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.46,0:05:00.41,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She could dim the lamp on the fence corner.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.41,0:05:03.66,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She could sound the shed's alarm on the girl's phone and send her running.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.66,0:05:05.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She held them both ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.74,0:05:07.09,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She dimmed nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.44,0:05:13.19,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Amy stood on the slope with her torch off and looked into the dark for a long time, eighteen metres from him now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.19,0:05:14.62,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Her pulse was steady.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.62,0:05:15.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Her hand was open.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.92,0:05:23.54,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then a shout came from the shed, Stavros's name in the guard's voice, and she turned on her own and went back up through the pines toward the fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.84,0:05:25.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was out by midnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.17,0:05:31.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The shed was a black frame with the tin roof fallen in, and the crew stood about in the steam with their helmets off.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.04,0:05:34.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Stavros sat down on the wet grass by the gas bottles.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.97,0:05:37.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}One of the crew shone a torch on him and swore.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.02,0:05:41.44,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}His eyebrows were gone, and the palms of both hands had risen in white blisters where he had held the valves.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.44,0:05:45.84,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Stavros turned them over in the light and looked at them with interest, the way he had always had to look, and laughed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.84,0:05:51.71,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then he undid the knot of the forepaws and slid the pelt off one shoulder, the left, to cool, as anyone would after a fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.97,0:05:56.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On PYTHIA's thermal feed the skin under it was as hot as the embers behind him.
